Plant-based diets are associated with lower levels of LDL cholesterol, a major risk factor for heart disease.
Research indicates that the high intake of whole foods in plant-based diets improves insulin sensitivity and reduces diabetes risk.
The abundance of antioxidants in plant-based diets helps neutralize free radicals, which are linked to cancer development.
Replacing animal products with plant-based alternatives can lead to significant reductions in inflammation, a key driver of chronic diseases.
Longitudinal studies have shown that populations with high plant-based food consumption have lower mortality rates from chronic diseases.